Teach JETLS's notebook support about Pluto notebooks as the VSCode Pluto
extension (juliapluto-pankgeorg.advanced-vscode-extension) presents them.

JETLS registers `notebookDocument/sync` for notebookType "jupyter-notebook"
only, so a client never syncs cells of any other notebook type and JETLS
serves nothing in them. The Pluto extension registers notebookType
"pluto-notebook" (contributes.notebooks in its package.json) with code cells
at languageId "julia" (`new NotebookCellData(..., "julia")` in its
deserializer) -- exactly the shape the added selector item matches. Nothing
downstream of the selector is Jupyter-specific: notebookType is stored on
NotebookInfo (types.jl:229, set at notebook.jl:192) and never branched on.

Deliberately NOT included: widening the URI-only `is_notebook_uri(uri::URI)`
check from `.ipynb` to also match `.pluto.jl`. It looks like the natural
companion -- a `.pluto.jl` open as a notebook is also a path JETLS picks up
as an ordinary script, so it can be analysed twice -- but it regresses the
nvim case. `is_abandoned_analysis_target` (analysis/full-analysis.jl:728)
reads `if (is_notebook_uri(uri) || ...) return !is_notebook_uri(state, uri)`,
and a `.pluto.jl` opened as a plain text buffer satisfies the widened URI
check while being absent from `notebook_cache`, so analysis is abandoned for
a file that currently works. `.ipynb` is safe there only because it is never
opened as text. If double analysis does show up in VSCode, fix it at the call
site in utils/server.jl, where `state` is in scope, not in the predicate.

Caveat worth knowing: JETLS analyses a notebook's cells concatenated in file
order, and Pluto's file order is presentation order, not reactive order.
Measured against an out-of-order notebook opened as a plain file, cross-cell
go-to-definition still resolved and no diagnostics were reported, so this is
less severe than it sounds -- but it is not nothing.

--- a/vendor/JETLSCore/src/notebook.jl
+++ b/vendor/JETLSCore/src/notebook.jl
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
         NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorItem(;
             notebook = "jupyter-notebook",
             cells = NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorCellsItem[
+                NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorCellsItem(; language = "julia")]),
+        NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorItem(;
+            notebook = "pluto-notebook",
+            cells = NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorCellsItem[
                 NotebookDocumentSyncOptionsNotebookSelectorCellsItem(; language = "julia")])]
 
 function notebook_document_sync_options()
